    "field": "Volcanic impacts on climate",
    "problem": "The paper addresses the challenge of quantifying the regional climate impact of large, non-explosive volcanic eruptions, as their tropospheric sulfur emissions create significant but uncertain radiative forcing effects by increasing the reflectivity of low-level clouds, which are difficult to validate with existing observational networks.",
    "method": "The paper uses global climate model simulations, comparing scenarios with and without volcanic sulphur dioxide emissions, to quantify the regional radiative forcing and potential climate impacts of the 2014 Nornahraun eruption in Iceland.",
    "task": "The task is to quantify the regional radiative forcing from the 2014 Nornahraun volcanic eruption in Iceland over the North Atlantic and Western Europe using global climate model simulations.",
